  "caveats": [
    "Two of the audit PDFs (ChainSecurity_dEURO_dEURO_audit.pdf and deuro_audit_report.pdf) were HEAD-verified but not parsed cover-to-cover. Per-contract coverage was reconstructed from filename + the upstream README's enumeration of dEURO-specific deltas. Operator should open both PDFs to confirm.",
    "Second-auditor identity unknown \u2014 deuro_audit_report.pdf does not name its auditor in the filename. Could be Decurity, Blockbite, or another independent reviewer.",
    "V3 internal audit is internal, not external. The 12-file markdown deliverable is thorough but it is self-authored by the dEURO team and should not be weighted as an external auditor's clean bill of health.",
    "emergencyStop quorum mechanics rely on nDEPS distribution. If a single party controls >10% of nDEPS, that party can unilaterally halt any bridge. The audit team should pull the nDEPS holder distribution before sizing this risk.",
    "DL TVL adapter has dead Frankencoin constants (MAINNET.WFPS, MAINNET.FPS, MAINNET.ZCHF). They are unused in the actual TVL math but a code-reading pipeline could be misled by their presence.",
    "L2 deployments rely on the OP-stack StandardBridge predeploy (0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000010). Out of scope for a dEURO-specific audit.",
    "Bridge horizon parameter: each StablecoinBridge has a constructor-set horizon (default 26 weeks). After horizon, the bridge cannot mint new dEURO (only burn/redeem). The first batch (2025-03-20 EURT, then 2025-04-23 EUROP/EURR/EURI) may already have passed their horizon as of 2026-05-15. Operator should pull horizon() on each of the 9 bridges to confirm which are still mint-active."
  ]
}